  "confounder_quality": 0.45,
  "rationale": "The query asks for underlying causes of longer resolution time while controlling for priority and category (both already in the table and named in the query, so not credited). The system supplies genuine candidate treatments surfaced from data (assignment_group_mismatch, resolver_is_assignee) plus contextual variables (issue_type, opened_hour, opened_on_weekend) that were NOT named in the query and could act as common causes of both the operational treatments and resolution time, demonstrating some real confounder surfacing. However, several of these are arguably weak or partly mediators (mismatch/resolver relationships), and resolution_hours and resolution_hours_vs_group_median are just re-expressions of the outcome rather than causes. The confounders are plausible but not strongly justified as adjusting for common causes of the treatments, so confounder quality is moderate."
}
